e that almost  uncompletable in a public game with no  communications but with the way the  systems and the most recent games are i  don't think they need to worry about  these unfortunate scenarios in the newer  entries in the series they haven't done  away with stealth exactly but it's  definitely taken a backseat compared to  its predecessors going for a more rpg  feel of a game as opposed to a stealth  game  because of the emphasis on rpg elements  like rarity and power systems  ubisoft has an excellent cooperative  experience on its hands in the form of  cooperative missions like in unity with  valhalla's mechanics or just straight up  cooperative dungeons like raids with  other players  it's a very typical idea that most games  have adopted but it can work as long as  they put the time into it  one obvious issue of having a co-op or  multiplayer mode is less time on the  single-player experience making both not  as good as they could be but assuming  they either have a dedicated team to  work on the multiplayer or  only one team working on both but are  given enough development time to flush  out both experiences  it could be an excellent time waster for  players who want to play more assassin's  creed but don't want to start new  playthroughs as they may find it boring  or repetitive  many companies have taken this approach  and succeeded but with the addition of a  separate company or team that means more  employees and  more money being spent by ubisoft to  fund the team so it's definitely a  double-edged sword there was an  interview with chief creative officer on  assassin's creed who talked about  wanting multiplayer back in the  franchise and said that with the current  modern technology they could have a  hundred players in the game at one time  assuming of course they removed the npcs  as that would be quite the performance  it who knows how far this development  idea has gone as this article was  published around 2018 before odyssey's  release so it probably won't be for a  long time until we see another  multiplayer co-op feature return again  as we wind down to the outro of the  video let me know your thoughts on the  video as a whole do you still play  assassin's creed was the multiplayer or  co-op  fun to you do you also want it back  anything like that feel free to share it  in the comments down below  as usual with this stuff like the video  if you enjoyed and subscribe for more  analysis and discussion videos on video  games in the near future i got plans to  release another one in the coming weeks  about another ubisoft series that was  also casually name dropped at the  beginning of this video  with that take care everyone and i'll  see you next time  [Music]  goodbye  [Music]  you
 

